# set test time
# Year is pinned (not left at TIME's own wall-clock default) so the
# Moon's own rendered position/phase - Moon3D.draw() runs on every
# frame, unlike the Sun-shading path views.svs's own comment covers -
# can't drift from one baseline regeneration to the next just because
# of which real year happens to be current when this runs (see
# funcs.MoonPosition's own comment on SHADE_EPOCH_DAY). 2026 matches
# terrain.svs's own pinned year, for one consistent year across this
# whole test suite rather than picking a different one per script.
Year 2026
Month 1
Day 15

# clear default model
Delete all

3d-model 7

Delete All Model2Ds

Tree1 m=0 x=10 y=10 z=0 h=20 degree=10 seed=0 r=0 tilt=60 twist=137.5 ratio=0.8 base=2 trunk=1 leaf=0.2
Tree1 m=0 x=-10 y=-25 z=0 h=20 degree=9 seed=0 r=0 tilt=60 twist=137.5 ratio=0.8 base=2 trunk=1 leaf=0.2

Tree2 m=10 x=25 y=10 z=0 h=20
Tree2 m=9 x=-10 y=-10 z=0 h=20

Delete All Sections
Section x=0 y=0 z=0 rx=0 ry=0 rz=0 resX=200 resY=200 -32,-32 32,-32 32,32 -32,32
Section x=0 y=16 z=0 rx=90 ry=0 rz=0 resX=200 resY=100 -32,-16 32,-16 32,16 -32,16
Section x=-16 y=0 z=0 rx=90 ry=0 rz=-90 resX=200 resY=100 -32,-16 32,-16 32,16 -32,16

Select nothing

Hide Sun Path
Hide Earth Surface
Shade.Real

ENLARGE3D
=======
S.E.

Select All Sections
Prebake Selected Sections
Process Active Impact on Selected Sections
Select nothing

REC.png solar-impacts-on-sections
